The initial data for B is different, since B is defined through the entire \
domain. We need to invert the function r(\[Rho]). This is a problem, since \
that is not invertible analytically.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9144063109384327`*^9, 
  3.914406370484404*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"452a491e-3b6f-4545-ac6b-\
17f5e1b8c1af"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"(*", 
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "uof\[Rho]", "]"}], "*)"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.915181203570277*^9, 3.915181210860166*^9}, {
   3.92156558415609*^9, 3.9215655848070803`*^9}, 3.928240224357874*^9, 
